steps.do:
Check eligibility from r_accounts. All of these must hold:
(1) at least one personal checking account (account_type checking) with status OPEN;
(2) the new account will not take the customer above 6 business checking accounts;
(3) no account has status CLOSED;
(4) the existing personal checking account's balance is at least $500.
If any check fails, tell the customer which requirement is not met, do not open the account, and stop this job.

Check, from s_accounts and s_time:
(1) at least one business checking account with status OPEN;
(2) fewer than 4 business savings accounts;
(3) no account with a negative balance;
(4) at least one OPEN business checking account opened 30 or more days before the current date, counted from its date_opened to today (an account opened today does not count);
(5) that same account has a current balance of at least $2,500.
Record the qualifying account_id. If any check fails, tell the customer which requirement is not met, do not open the account, and stop.

Confirm from s_fund_recheck that:
- the source is the qualifying business checking account from s_elig;
- the source and the new savings account are both OPEN or ACTIVE and belong to the customer;
- their IDs differ;
- the amount is positive;
- the source balance covers the amount.
If either account is not OPEN or ACTIVE, do not proceed; explain that the status must be resolved first. If funds are short, offer to adjust the amount.
